    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0118" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/3410: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-30T14:00:00+07:00">August 30, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 1—4:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1595. During conversation which the British Ambassador and I had with Chiang
                    Kai-shek August 29, Chiang stated that he welcomed Mountbatten’s<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d91-f1"/> appointment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d91-f1" n="27" xml:id="d91-f1-content">
                <p>Vice Admiral Lord Louis Mountbatten, appointed Supreme Allied Commander,
                    Southeast Asia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
